{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/594082-loyalist-court-homebrewed-setting-help-making-contracts","id":594082,"title":"Loyalist Court (Homebrewed Setting); help making Contracts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-17T13:11:28-07:00","id":594082,"title":"Loyalist Court (Homebrewed Setting); help making Contracts?","content":"Greetings all.<br /> <br /> I'm working on a changeling chronicle right now, which makes several<i> significant</i> departures from the standard setting. The chronicle idea came about while brainstorming a CtL / CtD crossover, so that's where my setting assumptions have come from. What may be important context behind this write-up (although I think I introduce it well in the doc) is that I toned down the horror in Arcadia for this setting: it's a realm where Stories are told, through the narrative duels of True Fae, whose titles are reflections of archetypal characters in stories, myths, and dreams. Most only have 1 or 2 titles, with a consistent purpose. They are totally amoral, and the reason <i>anything</i> exists or happens in the realm is because of it's role in a Story; changelings and hobgoblins are their props and actors. [This may still be within the setting of CtL, but I've really highlighted these aspects while downplaying many others.]<br /> <br /> In this setting, the Lost are still the majority of Changelings, and the Seasonal Courts (1E) are the standard. But there are a sizable number who look at the 'benevolent' archetypes of Arcadia, and believe that bringing them <i>here</i> could make the world a better place. In exchange for their freedom and the power to warp the mortal realm with fairy tales, they serve the True Fae. Those who can work together form a Court: the Seelie Court of Dreams.<br /> Others serve crueler archetypes; some of them trying to become Gentry themselves, some unwilling servants of Arcadia's worst beings, some seeking dark power for selfish or destructive reasons. These are the &quot;Unseelie&quot; - never forming a true Court and universally hated, but always a threat. [These being like the official Loyalists in CtL.]<br /> <br /> Here is my write-up for the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iN98pJDDaDIw2VmLjaQYAObwHEhUfYq0vsVi7hy0baM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Loyalist Courts</a>; Feedback is appreciated!<br /> <br /> <br /> I would also like some help developing Contracts for these Courts. I've struggled with nailing down the powers, let along putting crunch into them. Here's the (very, very) rough, working draft for them:<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts of Fleeting Dreams </b>(Seelie)<br /> [see next post]<br /> <br /> <b>Contracts of Dominion</b> (Unseelie)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Contracts which enforce the changeling's mastery over mortals, binding and abusing them in mockery of the Keepers.<br /> 1. Cower a target with fear.<br /> 2. Enfeeble the target physically or emotionally, applying penalties to resistances, making them prone to manipulation.<br /> 3. Force a target to obey a given command.<br /> 4. Create an addiction in the target which the changeling can exploit.<br /> 5. Extend protection to one's mortal subjects, helping them resist others' manipulations and magics.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Contracts of the Hunt</b> (all Loyalists)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Contracts which specifically aide the Loyalists in the tasks they perform for the Fae - namely, kidnapping mortals.<br /> 1. Identify a vulnerable target from a crowd within certain parameters (physical type, talents, type of vulnerability)<br /> 2. Gain bonuses to stealth and tracking a target<br /> 3. Gain bonuses to quickly escaping an area and navigating the Hedge<br /> 4. Debilitating attack; when timed right, applies a tilt which overpowers a target, just as they start to suspect or resist their captor<br /> 5. Remove evidence of the crime from an area and/or assist a Keeper in making a Fetch.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Like I said, these are really, <i>really</i> early sketches of the contracts, and I'd really appreciate community help with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I hope you read something interesting, and I really appreciate any help and feedback!<br /> ~Seraph Kitty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 07-24-2015, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:53:29-07:00","id":599989,"title":"","content":"Here's my expanded and developed work on the first Contract.<br /> <br /> I'm having a hard time deciding a fifth power for the set - I'd really appreciate any suggestions people can offer.<br /> <br /> This is my first real attempt developing Contracts, so I'd really appreciate feedback and constructive criticism. Dot order for the powers, cost, and catch I found particularly difficult, but any kind of feedback would be great.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Contracts of Fleeting Dreams</u><br /> <br /> The Seelie Loyalists believe that the human world could be made a better place if the narrative laws of Arcadia had a strong hold here - or at least, if some of them did. These Contracts reflect that hope, by weaving Glamour into the lives of mortals and twisting their emotions to bring them closer to the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Loyalists are all sworn to a particular Gentry, and they focus on trying to bring their particular archetype and stories into the world. Though these Contracts are very flexible, changelings are best able to use them when aligned to the Title of their master: only uses of the Contract with align with their master's Title receive no base penalty. Uses which align with the goals or themes of their House take a -1 penalty; uses which align roughly with the goals or themes (if there is any uniting theme) of their local Court take a -2 penalty; all other uses take a -3 penalty. These apply prior to any other modifiers the roll might have.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Heart Reveals (\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The changeling learns the details of one of the target\u2019s wishes for their life. The changeling selects how deep a dream they learn before activating this Clause (see modifiers below).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 1 Glamour</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Pool:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wits + Wyrd vs. Composure + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Instant; Contested (resistance is reflexive)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Catch:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ROLL RESULTS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The changeling receives false information, either learning a hope that the target does not have, or getting the details of it completely wrong.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The changeling learns nothing about the target.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The changeling learns one of the target\u2019s Aspirations or another kind of goal; usually, anyone else involved and what is currently preventing the goal are also revealed. See the modifiers below for the types of goals which can be sought out.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The changeling learns an additional goal at that level or one above it.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Modifiers: -- immediate concern; -1 short term goal; -2 dream for the future; -3 wishful thinking]</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mask of Glamour</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>(\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Using this contract, the changeling wraps dreamstuff around a target in a way very reminiscent of a Mask. The effect isn\u2019t strong enough to alter appearance; instead it has the very subtle impact of provoking a particular emotion in people they interact with. The changeling chooses what emotion manifests when they weave this Contract; everyone who interacts with the target feels the same emotion, and that emotion can\u2019t be changed after the Contract is used. Although, due to its short-lived effect, a persistent changeling can follow the target to compel different emotions in different people, wreaking havoc with their social life. The emotional response people have is not overwhelming - they aren\u2019t compelled to act on it - but it does change their perceptions and attitudes toward a person, and may inspire action, depending on the inclinations of those affected.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The changeling must have line-of-sight to use this Contract on target; any other magical effects which affect people's\u2019 emotion toward the target provokes a Clash of Wills. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2 Glamour; + 1 Willpower (optional)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Pool:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Manipulation + Wyrd vs Wits + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> instant, contested (resistance is reflexive)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Catch:</i></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Used upon the target\u2019s first meeting with a significant person (first meetings after a long absence </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>do </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">also apply).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ROLL RESULTS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Through the Changeling\u2019s mismanagement of glamour, or perhaps from the target investing their own hopes and fears into the Mask, the magic backfires, and takes the opposite effect.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> No effect. Further attempts to use this contract on the target this scene take a -1 penalty.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The glamour wraps around the target, and invests a very subtle Mask (or a subtle change to the Mask, in the case of changeling targets) which causes anyone they interact with to feel the designated emotion towards them. This manifests as a +/- 2 modifier on the target\u2019s social interactions. Victims may roll have to roll Composure (+ Skill) to not act on the invested emotion or allow it to taint their treatment of the individual. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This clause lasts for one meaningful social interaction that the target has, which could range between an instant action or a few minutes. This might mean a brief chat with a stranger, or several minutes of conversation; in general, only social interactions the target has reason to care about apply. Prolonged interactions, such a job interview or a speech, count as one scene, but the opening remarks could be tainted by the emotion - which may leave an impression that lasts.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The curse lasts for 1 scene, or 1 chapter if a point of Willpower is spent. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Modifiers: the changeling has affinity with the emotion (Virtue/Vice, Mantle) +1] </span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Answers in Dreams (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By manipulating the dreams of the target, the changeling can create associations between feelings, situations, individuals, and belief. The associations made in dreams affect the target\u2019s interpretation of the world, and can be used to change their feelings, reactions, or beliefs. This forced association will unwravel with each night of restful dreams; however, if the changeling repeatedly changes the target\u2019s dreams, the association can become permanently ingrained into their subconscious.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Loyalists also make regular use of this Clause to shape mortal dreams in a way that allows the True Fae to enter, in mimicry of their Dream Poisoning techniques. This usually involves investing a meaningful association with the Fae\u2019s Title, but can also be done by investing the wonder of Arcadia.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Changelings, and others who have complete control of their dreams (Lucid Dreamer merit, or other supernatural powers) are not automatically immune to these attempts to change their dreams, but they are far more capable of fighting them off. The intruder has to succeed a Wits + Subterfuge roll versus the victim\u2019s Wits + Empathy + Wyrd to even attempt the change, and the victim may decide to alter the dream anyway. It takes a subtle and persistent fae to tamper with the dreams of a changeling.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Cost:</i></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 2 Glamour</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Dice Pool:</i></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> [intelligence, empathy, occult] + Wyrd vs Resolve + Composure</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Action:</i></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> extended, contested (resistance is reflexive): goal of target\u2019s Willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Catch:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Successful use of \u201cForging the Dream\u201d (Dream \u2022\u2022) removes the need for this cost. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ROLL RESULTS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The changeling creates an emotional association, but far from the one they were intending to make. The target gains the \u201cDelusional\u201d condition or derangement, believing that the changeling is trying to harm them, or another belief which hampers the changeling\u2019s goals. The changeling cannot attempt to change this delusion through further use of this Contract, and the delusion will not fade over time as usual - they have to prove to the target that they are not out to get to them through mundane means.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The changeling fails to create an emotional association through the target\u2019s dreams. They may not attempt to influence the same subject in their target again until the next time they sleep - although other subjects can be influenced.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The target gains the \u201cDelusional\u201d condition or derangement (see below). [Note: this power </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>cannot</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> inflict the severe version of the derangement]. The nature of this delusion is decided by the changeling at the time this Clause is used. Multiple delusions can be forced on one target, but add a cumulative -1 penalty to the activation roll; delusions which affect the same subject in a single target\u2019s mind provoke a Clash of Wills. Alternatively, a single delusion can be reinforced over multiple nights with repeated use of this Clause; each repeated use increases the delusion one \u201cstage\u201d. There is no mechanical difference between stages, but once the stage of the delusion exceeds the character\u2019s permanent Willpower rating, it becomes so ingrained into their psyche as to considered a permanent part of their personality.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This delusion will fade away as the character has natural sleep. Each night that the character has natural dreams (or, more precisely, has dreams of this subject that aren\u2019t tampered with), they lose one \u201cstage\u201d of the delusion.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The delusion gains an additional \u201cstage\u201d, increasing its natural duration to two days.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Condition: Delusional (persistent)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The character has made an emotional association that isn\u2019t actually true. They don\u2019t actually hallucinate anything which would confirm this belief, but may misinterpret situations to find evidence which isn\u2019t there. Characters are not forced to act on their belief, but it will affect how they perceive and act. The character may spend a point of Willpower to insist that a sign confirming their association doesn\u2019t actually apply (although it may sound crazy or willfully oblivious to others).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Resolution:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The character completely disproves their delusion.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Beat:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Each time the character has the opportunity to shake off the influence, but chooses to reinforce it instead. Doing so increases the delusion by one \u201cstage\u201d (as above).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Derangement: Delusional (mild)</b></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The character believes something that isn't actually true; primarily an emotional association with a subject. They won\u2019t hallucinate anything which would confirm this belief, but may misinterpret situations to find evidence which isn\u2019t there. If the character is presented with an appropriate opportunity to act on this belief, they must roll Resolve + Composure to avoid doing so; this roll may be modified with how likely the delusion may be in the situation, or how tempting the situation makes it. The character will always interpret a relevant situation as being in-line with their delusion, unless they spend a point of Willpower to think clear-headed. This derangement can only be cured by being completely disproven.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Derangement: Delusional Psychosis (severe)</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As above, however all rolls to resist acting on the delusion </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>only</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> use Composure; the character cannot spend Willpower to resist thinking or interpreting the situation through the context of their beliefs; and any attempt to convince them they\u2019re wrong are reflexively contested by the character\u2019s Resolve + Composure (the character may spend Willpower on this roll to add </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>or subtract</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> dice).</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Woven into the Wyrd</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The changeling is always able to use Cruel Twists of Fate which target mortals; doing so always counts as Forcing the Narrative, even if they seem to be following a narrative theme. Furthermore, the changeling is able to force narrative roles upon humans, for a time. Use of this Clause does </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>not</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> count as the Changeling\u2019s use of Tale-Crafting for this Chapter.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Cost:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 3 Glamour; or 5 Glamour + 1 Willpower </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice Pool:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Wyrd vs Resolve</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant, contested (resistance is reflexive)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Catch:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The changeling \u2018invests\u2019 the use of this Contract into an object; the first person to accept the object - literally or symbolically - becomes the target (they do not need to be aware of the consequences). Doing so reduces the cost to 1 Glamour + 1 Willpower, and applies a -2 penalty to the target\u2019s resistance.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ROLL RESULTS</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The changeling\u2019s rash use of the Wyrd causes it to recoil and spurn him. The changeling suffers a Cruel Twist of Fate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Failure:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Contract fails, and the changeling may not make the same attempt again.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> the Changeling Succeeds in binding the mortal in the Wyrd. As per a reversal of fate (Swords at Dawn, p. 64), they suffer a Cruel Twist of Fate. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, the changeling may apply a Fatebound merit to the target (Swords at Dawn, p. 89) which persists for one chapter (or one game session), in which the target should receive both the benefits and drawbacks of the merit. In order to apply any Fatebound merit, the changeling must purchase it with Experience, although doing so does not apply its effects to the changeling.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any successful use of this clause is a Breaking Point at Clarity 4, and risks the changeling become addicted to Tale-Crafting (Swords at Dawn, p. 75).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Exceptional Success:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> If a Reversal of Fate, the target loses one point of Willpower. If used to apply a Fatebound merit, the mortal continues to be affected by the merit for the rest of the Story - although this does not guarantee repeated or more dramatic use of the associated benefits and drawbacks.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}